---
import KnowledgeLayout from '../../layouts/KnowledgeLayout.astro';
import WorkflowDiagram from '../../components/docs/WorkflowDiagram.astro';
import FAQ from '../../components/seo/FAQ.astro';
import RelatedDocs from '../../components/docs/RelatedDocs.astro';
const toc=[{id:'install',label:'Install'},{id:'quick-start',label:'Quick start'},{id:'inputs',label:'Inputs'},{id:'files',label:'Multiple files'},{id:'recipes',label:'Workflow recipes'},{id:'output',label:'Use the output'},{id:'troubleshooting',label:'Troubleshooting'},{id:'privacy',label:'Runtime boundary'}];
const starterWorkflow=`{
  "name": "TokenCalculator preflight",
  "nodes": [
    { "parameters": {}, "id": "manual-trigger", "name": "Run workflow", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger", "typeVersion": 1, "position": [240, 300] },
    { "parameters": { "jsCode": "return [{ json: { text: 'Summarize this customer message in three bullets.' } }];" }, "id": "sample-text", "name": "Sample text", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "typeVersion": 2, "position": [460, 300] },
    { "parameters": { "operation": "count", "source": "text", "text": "={{ $json.text }}", "modelId": "gpt-5.6-terra" }, "id": "token-calculator", "name": "Token Calculator", "type": "@jay0073/n8n-nodes-tokencalculator.tokenCalculator", "typeVersion": 1, "position": [700, 300] }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Run workflow": { "main": [[{ "node": "Sample text", "type": "main", "index": 0 }]] },
    "Sample text": { "main": [[{ "node": "Token Calculator", "type": "main", "index": 0 }]] }
  },
  "settings": {}
}`;
const outputExample=`{
  "operation": "count",
  "source": { "characters": 58, "files": [] },
  "result": {
    "modelId": "gpt-5.6-terra",
    "inputTokens": 12,
    "outputTokens": 0,
    "cost": { "input": 0.000024, "output": 0, "total": 0.000024 },
    "context": { "ratio": 0.000011, "remaining": 1049988, "overContext": false }
  }
}`;
const faq=[
  {q:'Can n8n count tokens before calling OpenAI, Claude, Gemini, or DeepSeek?',a:'Yes. Place Token Calculator before the provider node, map the final text or files, and use its inputTokens, cost, and context fields to decide whether the request should continue.'},
  {q:'How do I count multiple files from an n8n Form Trigger?',a:'Choose a binary input mode and set Binary Properties to * for every upload, a prefix wildcard such as uploads*, or an explicit comma-separated list of binary properties.'},
  {q:'Does the n8n token calculator upload my prompt?',a:'No content is sent to TokenCalculator.dev. Calculation runs inside the n8n runtime, although n8n execution logs and retention settings still apply.'},
  {q:'Can the node read PDF or DOCX files?',a:'Not directly. Extract PDF or DOCX text with an earlier n8n node and map that output into the Text field.'},
];
const faqSchema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'FAQPage',mainEntity:faq.map(item=>({'@type':'Question',name:item.q,acceptedAnswer:{'@type':'Answer',text:item.a}}))};
---
<KnowledgeLayout title="TokenCalculator n8n Community Node Documentation" description="Install and use the TokenCalculator n8n community node for text, multiple files, images, token counting, cost estimates, and model comparisons." heading="TokenCalculator for n8n" eyebrow="Docs · Automation" datePublished="2026-08-28" dateModified="2026-09-01" section="Documentation" type="TechArticle" keywords={['n8n token calculator','n8n community node','n8n form multiple files','LLM cost workflow']} {toc}>
  <p class="knowledge-lead">Add a local preflight step before an LLM call. The node can count mapped text, combine multiple text or source files, apply provider image-token formulas, estimate cost, and compare models without sending the input to TokenCalculator.dev.</p>

  <h2>What is an n8n token calculator?</h2>
  <p>An n8n token calculator is a workflow step that measures an LLM request before the paid model call. TokenCalculator turns prompts, form uploads, source files, and images into an input-token count, context-window usage, and model cost estimate. It fits AI agents, document-processing forms, support automation, content pipelines, and any n8n workflow that needs a predictable token or spending limit.</p>
  <WorkflowDiagram title="LLM request preflight" caption="Measure the exact payload after extraction and before the provider call; branch on token, context, or cost fields." steps={[{label:'Trigger or form',detail:'Text and uploads',tone:'source'},{label:'Prepare content',detail:'Extract or combine',tone:'source'},{label:'Token Calculator',detail:'Count and estimate',tone:'measure'},{label:'IF guard',detail:'Budget or context',tone:'decision'},{label:'LLM node',detail:'Approved inputs',tone:'action'}]}/>

  <h2 id="install">Install the community node</h2>
  <ol><li>In n8n, open <strong>Settings → Community nodes</strong>.</li><li>Select <strong>Install</strong> and enter <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@jay0073/n8n-nodes-tokencalculator"><code>@jay0073/n8n-nodes-tokencalculator</code></a>.</li><li>Accept n8n's community-node notice, install the package, then search the node picker for <strong>Token Calculator</strong>.</li></ol>
  <p>Use version <strong>0.1.5 or later</strong> for multiple-file Form Trigger support. If your deployment manages community packages through environment variables, the UI cannot remove or update them; change the deployment configuration and restart n8n instead.</p>

  <h2 id="quick-start">Quick start: dynamic text</h2>
  <ol><li>Add a <strong>Manual Trigger</strong>, then an <strong>Edit Fields</strong> or <strong>Code</strong> node that outputs a field named <code>text</code>.</li><li>Add <strong>Token Calculator</strong> and choose <strong>Count Tokens</strong>.</li><li>Set <strong>Input Source</strong> to <strong>Text</strong>.</li><li>Set <strong>Text</strong> to <code>{'{{ $json.text }}'}</code>, choose a model, and execute the step.</li></ol>
  <div class="technical-callout"><span>Dynamic expression</span><code>{'{{ $json.text }}'}</code><span>Nested webhook field</span><code>{'{{ $json.body.prompt }}'}</code></div>
  <p>The expression must resolve to a real field in the incoming item. If the input panel shows <code>undefined</code>, inspect the previous node's JSON and drag the correct field into <strong>Text</strong>.</p>
  <h3>Importable starter workflow</h3><p>Copy this JSON, choose <strong>Import from clipboard</strong> in n8n, and run it. The community node must already be installed.</p>
  <pre class="docs-code"><code>{starterWorkflow}</code></pre>

  <h2 id="inputs">Choose the right input mode</h2>
  <ul><li><strong>Text:</strong> mapped prompts, messages, database fields, webhook bodies, or text assembled by an earlier Code node.</li><li><strong>Binary File:</strong> one or more incoming text/source/data files or supported images.</li><li><strong>Text and Binary File:</strong> combines mapped text with every selected binary file into one measurement.</li></ul>
  <p>Readable text formats include TXT, Markdown, JSON, CSV, common source-code formats, HTML/XML, YAML, SQL, shell scripts, and logs. Images include PNG, JPEG, GIF, and WebP. Each file is limited to 10 MB. PDF and DOCX extraction is not performed by this node; extract their text in an earlier node and map the result through <strong>Text</strong>.</p>

  <h2 id="files">Form Trigger and multiple files</h2>
  <p>n8n stores Form Trigger uploads as binary properties. A multi-file field commonly becomes several properties with numeric suffixes. Token Calculator supports all of them:</p>
  <ol><li>In <strong>Form Trigger</strong>, add a <strong>File</strong> field and enable multiple-file upload.</li><li>Connect it directly to <strong>Token Calculator</strong>.</li><li>Choose <strong>Binary File</strong> or <strong>Text and Binary File</strong>.</li><li>Set <strong>Binary Properties</strong> to <code>*</code> for every incoming file. Use <code>uploads*</code> for properties beginning with <code>uploads</code>, or a comma-separated list such as <code>contract0,contract1</code>.</li></ol>
  <div class="technical-callout"><span>All files</span><code>*</code><span>One field prefix</span><code>uploads*</code><span>Explicit properties</span><code>document0,document1,image0</code></div>
  <p>All readable text files are joined with blank lines. Every supported image contributes its own token allocation. The output's <code>source.files</code> array records each filename, size, extraction method, and n8n binary property.</p>
  <WorkflowDiagram title="Multiple Form Trigger uploads" caption="The Form Trigger keeps several uploads on one n8n item as separate binary properties. A wildcard collects them into one measurement." steps={[{label:'n8n Form',detail:'Allow multiple files',tone:'source'},{label:'Binary properties',detail:'uploads0, uploads1…',tone:'source'},{label:'Selector: uploads*',detail:'Resolve every match',tone:'measure'},{label:'Combined result',detail:'Text + every image',tone:'action'}]}/>

  <h2 id="recipes">Useful workflow recipes</h2>
  <h3>Reject an oversized prompt before the LLM</h3><div class="technical-callout"><span>Flow</span><code>Webhook → Token Calculator → IF → LLM</code><span>IF expression</span><code>{'{{ $json.result.context.overContext }}'}</code></div><p>Send the <code>false</code> branch to the LLM. Route the <code>true</code> branch to a chunking step, storage, or a clear error response.</p>
  <h3>Apply a token budget</h3><p>In an IF node, compare <code>{'{{ $json.result.inputTokens }}'}</code> with your limit—for example, <code>100000</code>. This is useful when your operational limit is smaller than the model's maximum context window.</p>
  <h3>Compare model cost before routing</h3><p>Choose <strong>Compare Models</strong>, select candidate models, and set <strong>Expected Output Tokens</strong>. Inspect each row in <code>result</code> and route based on <code>cost.total</code>.</p>

  <h2 id="output">Understand and reuse the output</h2>
  <pre class="docs-code"><code>{outputExample}</code></pre>
  <ul><li><code>result.inputTokens</code>: measured input tokens.</li><li><code>result.cost.total</code>: estimated total USD cost.</li><li><code>result.context.remaining</code>: tokens remaining in the selected model's context window.</li><li><code>result.context.overContext</code>: ready-to-use boolean for an IF node.</li><li><code>source.files</code>: audit metadata for every processed upload.</li></ul>
  <p>OpenAI-compatible text uses local BPE tokenization. Other provider families are deterministic estimates; images use provider formulas. Provider billing remains authoritative.</p>

  <h2 id="troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</h2>
  <ul><li><strong>Text shows undefined:</strong> execute the previous node and map a field visible in its output.</li><li><strong>No files were counted:</strong> choose a binary input mode and use <code>*</code>, the correct prefix wildcard, or exact property names.</li><li><strong>Unsupported file type:</strong> extract it first, then pass plain text. PDF/DOCX bytes are not guessed as UTF-8.</li><li><strong>Package cannot be edited in the UI:</strong> it was installed through deployment environment variables.</li><li><strong>Old behavior after updating:</strong> confirm version <code>0.1.5</code> or later, restart n8n, and reopen the editor.</li></ul>

  <FAQ items={faq.map(item=>({question:item.q,answer:item.a}))} compact />

  <h2 id="privacy">Runtime boundary</h2><p>Processing occurs inside your n8n runtime. The node requires no TokenCalculator.dev account or API key and does not send workflow content to TokenCalculator.dev. Your deployment still controls execution-data retention, logs, storage, credentials, and access.</p>
  <p><a href="https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/community-nodes/installation/">n8n installation documentation</a> · <a href="/docs/activepieces/">Activepieces guide</a> · <a href="/integrations/">All integrations</a></p>
  <RelatedDocs hrefs={['/docs/activepieces/','/docs/api/','/docs/files/']} />
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />
</KnowledgeLayout>
